content.text:
Rewrite lcd_status.c using BSP. Need to know the BSP function names:
- `BSP_LCD_Init()`
- `BSP_LCD_LayerDefaultInit(uint16_t LayerIndex, uint32_t FB_Address)`
- `BSP_LCD_SelectLayer(uint32_t LayerIndex)`
- `BSP_LCD_SetLayerVisible(uint32_t LayerIndex, FunctionalState state)`
- `BSP_LCD_SetFont(sFONT *pFonts)`
- `BSP_LCD_SetTextColor(uint32_t Color)`
- `BSP_LCD_SetBackColor(uint32_t Color)`
- `BSP_LCD_Clear(uint32_t Color)`
- `BSP_LCD_DisplayStringAt(uint16_t X, uint16_t Y, uint8_t *pText, Text_AlignModeTypdef mode)`
- `BSP_LCD_DisplayStringAtLine(uint16_t Line, uint8_t *ptr)`
- `LCD_FRAME_BUFFER` macro.
- `LCD_COLOR_WHITE`, `LCD_COLOR_BLACK`, `LCD_COLOR_GREEN`, `LCD_COLOR_RED`, `LCD_COLOR_BLUE`.
- `CENTER_MODE`.
- `Font12`/`Font24`.

Implementation:
```
void LCD_Status_Init(void) {
  BSP_LCD_Init();
  BSP_LCD_LayerDefaultInit(0, LCD_FRAME_BUFFER);
  BSP_LCD_SelectLayer(0);
  BSP_LCD_SetLayerVisible(0, ENABLE);
  BSP_LCD_SetFont(&Font12);
  BSP_LCD_SetTextColor(LCD_COLOR_BLACK);
  BSP_LCD_SetBackColor(LCD_COLOR_WHITE);
  BSP_LCD_Clear(LCD_COLOR_WHITE);
  LCD_Status_SetCardPresent(0);
}
void LCD_Status_SetCardPresent(int present) {
  BSP_LCD_SetFont(&Font12);
  BSP_LCD_SetBackColor(LCD_COLOR_WHITE);
  BSP_LCD_Clear(LCD_COLOR_WHITE);
  BSP_LCD_SetTextColor(LCD_COLOR_BLUE);
  BSP_LCD_DisplayStringAt(0, 10, (uint8_t*)TEXT_VERSION, CENTER_MODE);
  BSP_LCD_SetTextColor(present ? LCD_COLOR_GREEN : LCD_COLOR_RED);
  BSP_LCD_DisplayStringAt(0, 30, (uint8_t*)(present ? TEXT_PRESENT : TEXT_ABSENT), CENTER_MODE);
}
```
- `BSP_LCD_DisplayStringAt` uses the `BackColor` for the character background; the clear white sets the screen white. Good.
- `BSP_LCD_SetFont(&Font12)`: Font12 is defined in App/Src/font12.c; the BSP header declares it. Good.
- Maybe `BSP_LCD_DisplayStringAt` with `CENTER_MODE` computes `X` based on text width; passing X=0 is okay. It may use `BSP_LCD_GetXSize()`.
- The version line text length 28*7=196; centered in 240.
- The card line 20*7=140; centered.
- We can use `Font12` from App. If the linker complains about Font12 duplicate with Utilities? We only compile App/font12.c; Utilities/font12.c not compiled. Good.
- `BSP_LCD_Clear` uses `FillBuffer` with DMA2D; DMA2D enabled.
