content.text:
#### 3. PA10 runtime config in `SD_Monitor_Init`

Even if CubeMX regenerates output, we reconfigure input. Add a static `SD_GPIO_Init` in `sd_monitor.c`:
```
static void SD_GPIO_Init(void) {
  GPIO_InitTypeDef gpio = {0};
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOA_CLK_ENABLE();
  gpio.Pin = GPIO_PIN_10;
  gpio.Mode = GPIO_MODE_INPUT;
  gpio.Pull = GPIO_PULLDOWN;
  gpio.Speed = GPIO_SPEED_FREQ_LOW;
  HAL_GPIO_Init(GPIOA, &gpio);
}
```
Call at start of `SD_Monitor_Init`. This ensures input even if generated output. The card detect active-high; pull-down. If the module is active-low, this will read high (present) when disconnected; but the user observed active-high. Fine.
Add.

