Implement `sd_test.c`. Need `sd_card.h` for `hsd`, `log_uart.h`. Use `HAL_SD_WriteBlocks`/`ReadBlocks`. Need `string.h` for memset? We'll fill buffer with loop.

`SD_TestWriteSpeed`:
```c
static uint32_t sd_test_buffer[1024] __attribute__((aligned(4)));
#define SD_TEST_CHUNK_BLOCKS 8U
static void SD_Test_Fill(uint32_t pattern) { for (i=0;i<1024;i++) sd_test_buffer[i]=pattern; }
static uint32_t SD_Test_Kbps(uint32_t blocks, uint32_t ms) { if(ms==0) ms=1; return (blocks*512U*1000U)/(ms*1024U); }
```
`SD_TestWriteSpeed`:
```
if (!result || block_count==0) return 0;
memset(result,0,sizeof(*result));
result->start_lba=start_lba; result->block_count=block_count;
uint32_t start=HAL_GetTick();
for (offset=0; offset<block_count; ) {
  chunk = min(8, block_count-offset);
  SD_Test_Fill(0x5AA5AA55U ^ offset);
  if (HAL_SD_WriteBlocks(&hsd, sd_test_buffer, start_lba+offset, chunk, 5000U) != HAL_OK) { LOG_Printf("SD:TEST_WRITE_FAIL err=%lu\r\n", hsd.ErrorCode); return 0; }
  offset += chunk;
}
result->write_ms = HAL_GetTick()-start; if 0 -> 1;
result->write_kbs = SD_Test_Kbps(block_count, result->write_ms);
LOG_Printf("SD:TEST_WRITE blocks=%lu bytes=%lu time=%lu ms speed=%lu KB/s\r\n", ...);
return 1;
```
`SD_TestReadSpeed` similar, just read.
`SD_TestReadWrite`:
```
