Replace the write block with a retry loop:

```c
    LOG_Write("SD:PARTITIONS_CREATE (erases partition table)\r\n");

    {
        HAL_StatusTypeDef write_status = HAL_ERROR;
        uint32_t retry;

        for (retry = 0U; retry < 3U; ++retry)
        {
            if (!SD_WaitReady(2000U))
            {
                /* Card may be left in a data state by a previous failed
                 * transfer: reinitialize it. */
                (void)SD_Card_InitAtClock(SD_CLOCK_DIV);
            }

            write_status = HAL_SD_WriteBlocks_DMA(&hsd, (uint8_t *)mbr, 0U, 1U);
            if (write_status == HAL_OK && SD_WaitTransfer(5000U))
            {
                break;
            }
            LOG_Printf("SD:CREATE_WRITE_RETRY %lu err=%lu\r\n", ...);
            (void)SD_WaitReady(1000U);
            HAL_Delay(50U);
        }

        if (write_status != HAL_OK) { ... return 0; }
    }
```

Hmm, SD_Card_InitAtClock re-inits the card at SD_CLOCK_DIV but the sweep might have changed it. In practice fine.

Careful: SD_Card_InitAtClock is defined above SD_CreatePartitions in the file (yes, line ~75). Good.

