OH WAIT. I bet I know: The FatFs format later wrote to LBA 2048+ and succeeded. The MBR write at LBA 0: maybe it succeeded, but then our verify read used the DMA into `verify[128]`, and the data was fine... but memcmp compares mbr vs verify. Hmm, if the read returned the new MBR, they'd match.

